Sanitation without a sewer is still a complete service (@wu-decentralized: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @water-and-sanitation, #water-and-sanitation "A-reproducible-collection-and-stormwater-study.lingua#r_2A8HPWPTS3A5BWCJWCA6C3JTCP") { r_2EFRBEDV2CAQGYY6SAQ8FAJ8YM
**Read:** [Faecal Sludge Management — Strande, Ronteltap and Brdjanovic](../sources/Faecal-Sludge-Management-Eawag.lingua#r_2CSTH41F4C2WWARQ7X0ZF5NNGY) as a complete book, alongside the relevant household sanitation material in [Manual de Saneamento — Funasa, fifth edition](../sources/Manual-de-Saneamento-Funasa.lingua#r_65G5YY3QVCA8HAXMPC8RTPKEWE) and [Sanitation safety planning — WHO, second edition](../sources/Sanitation-Safety-Planning-WHO.lingua#r_2FF0R519TGR5RNY3EVV7APPZ86). Follow containment and transport through their whole downstream chain.

A local tank, pit or other containment system changes where material waits and how it reaches treatment. Stored faecal sludge can differ greatly from fresh dilute sewage. The dimensions of a container alone do not establish infiltration performance, hygienic emptying, transport availability or a receiving facility's ability to accept the delivered load.

**Work:** Compare a hypothetical sewered neighbourhood and one served by scheduled emptying. Track users, water, sludge, access, vehicle trips, treatment acceptance, costs and service interruption. Account for a missed collection and an unexpectedly concentrated delivery. Include a receiving site's sampling and acceptance evidence instead of assuming each truck carries interchangeable liquid.

Map exposure for users, workers and neighbours using published cases and the sanitation planning reference. This is a documentary and calculation exercise; entering confined spaces, opening hazardous containment or handling untreated material requires appropriate professional arrangements. For advanced study, combine transport scheduling with variable quantities, treatment limits and actual service records. Compare the proposed system against a period withheld from calibration.

**Continue:** [A reproducible collection and stormwater study](A-reproducible-collection-and-stormwater-study.lingua#r_2A8HPWPTS3A5BWCJWCA6C3JTCP).
